.TH SYNORA-SERVER 1 "June 2026" "Synora Studio 1.0" "Synora AI Core Commands"
.SH NAME
synora-server \- Synora Studio Headless AI Inference Engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python server.py
[\-\-host \fIHOST\fR] [\-\-port \fIPORT\fR] [\-\-model \fIMODEL\fR] [\-\-api-manager]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synora-server
is the high-performance AI inference engine and routing core for Synora Studio. It provides the REST/WebSocket interface for LLM chunking, embeddings, agent execution, and memory management.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIHOST\fR
Bind the inference API to the specified host. (Default: 0.0.0.0)
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Bind the inference API to the specified port. (Default: 5000)
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIMODEL\fR
Specify the underlying local model string to load into VRAM or the endpoint gateway path.
.TP
.B \-\-api-manager
Launch the interactive API Key Administration Wizard to manage BYOK (Bring Your Own Key) profiles.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the engine on port 8080:
.B python server.py --port 8080
.SH AUTHOR
Synora Studio Framework
